<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shukkeien</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shukkeien is a Japanese landscape garden in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiroshima">Hiroshima</a>, begun in 1620 for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asano-nagaakira">Asano Nagaakira</a>, the first Asano lord of the Hiroshima domain, by his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tea">tea</a> master Ueda Sōko. Its name means 'shrunken-scenery garden', as it recreates famous landscapes in miniature around a central pond. It was destroyed by the atomic bomb in 1945 and later restored.</p></div>
